---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Seam from '../components/Seam.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { principles } from '../data/principles';
import { workAreas } from '../data/work';
import profile from '../portrait-2026-10.avif';
---

<Base
  profile
  title="About"
  description="Who Antonio Rodríguez Martínez is, how he works, and the principles behind the work: a technical program manager and former CTO who still writes code."
>
  <section class="hero hero--about">
    <div class="hero__title">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>Who I am</h1>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero__avatar-frame">
      <Image
        class="hero__avatar"
        src={profile}
        alt={SITE.portraitAlt}
        width={224}
        height={224}
        widths={[80, 112, 160, 224]}
        sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 112px, 80px"
        format="avif"
        quality={50}
        fit="cover"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </figure>
    <p class="hero__intro">
      I'm Antonio Rodríguez Martínez. Technical program manager at Stanley Black &amp; Decker, and a
      former CTO. I still write code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Seam />

  <section class="section prose" id="work">
    <h2>At work</h2>
    <p>
      I'm a member of SBD Digital, the team behind Stanley Black &amp; Decker's websites and apps and the
      services behind them. I joined in 2021, and I'm one of the technical people in our product design
      group. The title has changed a few times; the work goes where the most important problem is.
    </p>
    <ul class="areas">
      {
        workAreas.map((area) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{area.title}.</strong> {area.body}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      I enjoy this work a lot. Our team is truly diverse and respectful, toward each other and toward the
      work, and I'm proud of what we do.
    </p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/projects#work-for-others">What I built there</a></p>
  </section>

  <Seam />

  <section class="section prose" id="background">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      I wrote my first HTML around age nine, on a WebTV, from books I talked my dad into buying. Paid work started with a bootstrapped web agency in college, with a friend. We learned to write clean
      code and to manage client projects. A marketing firm acquired us, and I built custom solutions
      under tight deadlines. Since then I have worked as a full-stack developer, architect, CTO, and
      engineering manager, and now as a technical program manager at a global hardware company.
    </p>
    <p>
      Along the way I came to one belief: technical excellence works best with strong team dynamics and
      psychological safety.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Seam />

  <section class="section" id="how-i-work">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I listen first and map how things really are. Then I make the smallest honest plan, build it,
        ship it, and teach the team to keep it running.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="principles" id="principles">
      {
        principles.map((principle) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{principle.title}</h3>
            <p>{principle.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Seam />

  <section class="section prose" id="daily">
    <h2>Daily</h2>
    <p>
      I write almost daily: essays, ideas, documentation. I move every day. I run wherever I am, and I
      love it; I also play basketball, lift weights, and train in martial arts. I cook whole foods, and
      I'm a hands-on parent to three kids. I've rebuilt my life post-divorce and learned that
      presence and execution matter more than perfection.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Seam />

  <section class="section prose" id="company">
    <h2>The company</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={SITE.company.url}>{SITE.company.name} LLC</a> is my company. It is the door for{' '}
      <a href={SITE.company.consultingUrl}>consulting</a> now and soap later, and it publishes the picture
      books I wrote for my kids. <a href={SITE.notesUrl}>Notes</a> is mine, not the company's.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, or on{' '}
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/antoniwan" rel="me">LinkedIn</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/antoniwan" rel="me">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
